        "original_id": "0336cec6-ecce-5c3a-b5c2-5fcd59a2f70e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Terry Riley\n- Works: Persian Surgery Dervishes, A Rainbow in Curved Air, In C\n- Places: Los Angeles, Paris\n- Topics: minimalist music, avant-garde music\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Riley was born on June 24, 1935.\n- Terry Riley is an American composer and performing musician associated with the minimalist school of Western classical music and is regarded as one of its pioneers.\n- Terry Riley released earlier works titled In C and A Rainbow in Curved Air before Persian Surgery Dervishes.\n- Persian Surgery Dervishes is a recording by Terry Riley of two live solo electric organ concerts.\n- The first concert recorded on Persian Surgery Dervishes was held in Los Angeles on April 18, 1971.\n- The second concert recorded on Persian Surgery Dervishes was held in Paris on May 24, 1972.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
